From c67d3db69e2e432c11f1a56bdee689ffcd40e956 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gregory P. Smith" <68491+gpshead@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:46:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [3.14] gh-160310: Fix quadratic one-shot `decompress()` with
 many members (GH-160311) (#161038)

gzip.decompress(), bz2.decompress(), lzma.decompress() and
compression.zstd.decompress() handed each new decompressor all of the
remaining input and copied the rest back through unused_data, so input
made of many concatenated members took quadratic time.  Each member is
now fed in chunks that start at 1 KiB and double, and the loop steps
back over unused_data by offset.  The first chunk is the whole input,
so single-member data still takes one decompressor call.

bz2, lzma and zstd share the loop through a private helper in
compression._common._streams; gzip keeps its own because it parses the
member header, trailer and padding itself.

ANT-2026-9R8SO5S2

(cherry picked from commit e80962a4bd68b162a54fc63cfb754237c2f81d8e)
Upstream: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/c67d3db69e2e432c11f1a56bdee689ffcd40e956
